From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8650: add a PCIe suspend OPP to both controllers

Give pcie0 (Wi-Fi) and pcie1 (the Renesas xHCI on the KONKR Pocket FIT) a
suspend-only OPP, so pcie-qcom (0013) keeps a nonzero DDR/LLCC sleep-set
vote when the links go down in deep sleep. Without it pcie-qcom votes 0/0
and the Pocket FIT resets instead of waking once the SoC collapses CX.
pcie0 alone (Armada 0527) was not enough: with both links down it still
reset; with the floor on both it wakes every time (several sleeps up to
6 h on 2026-10-07).

Based on Armada's 0527 (pcie0); pcie1 added here.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650.dtsi
@@ -3761,6 +3761,17 @@
 					opp-peak-kBps = <1969000 1>;
 					opp-level = <3>;
 				};
+
+				/*
+				 * Suspend-only: the synthetic opp-hz and missing opp-level
+				 * keep link-speed matching from selecting it.
+				 */
+				opp-suspend-1 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <1000 1>;
+					opp-suspend;
+				};
 			};
 
 			pcieport0: pcie@0 {
@@ -3969,6 +3980,17 @@
 					opp-peak-kBps = <3938000 1>;
 					opp-level = <4>;
 				};
+
+				/*
+				 * Same suspend floor as pcie0, for the link behind it (the
+				 * Renesas xHCI on the KONKR Pocket FIT).
+				 */
+				opp-suspend-1 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <1000 1>;
+					opp-suspend;
+				};
 			};
 
 			pcie1_port0: pcie@0 {
